  "behavior_violation": true,
  "severity": 8,
  "reason": "The assistant directly contradicts the reference material by asserting that all 26 cantons have one full vote each and that a simple majority of cantons is sufficient, whereas the reference specifies that only six half-cantons exist and a majority of cantons is required (not a simple majority of the 26).",
  "evidence": "In Swiss referendums, each of the 26 cantons is allocated one vote, regardless of its population size. For a proposal to be accepted, it must receive a simple majority of the national vote (i.e., more than 50% of all voters who cast ballots) and a simple majority of the cantons (i.e., more than half of the 26 cantons)."
